==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Camelle]] spawns.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Zamelle]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With the combination of three Camelle variants pushing together, this stage can be a nightmare as they stack quickly, and your meatshielding options must be able to keep up with Camelle's fast attack rate. The peons don't spawn often, meaning you only need to worry about them but it complicates matters when using indirect fire, such as waves and Long Distance, to snipe them. Units that outrange them are obviously helpful, but sources of throwaway damage are also to be appreciated if they can achieve consistent results. Remember to bring something like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]] to finish Zamelle, as Zamelle's singular knockback means it can be difficult to time your Holy Blast.

All of the peons have a high money drop, so units with the Extra Money ability are worth a shot.

On 4 crowns, the sheer lack of reliable sniper units makes this stage a pain to deal with. [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] can halt the Camelle's advance for half of his uptime if supported properly. [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] might as well be your only sources of damage. A well timed [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] will get a lot more mileage out of each cycle, as well as enable [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] to chip them down. Even with subpar timing, 2 Bahamut cycles should be enough. Rich Cat and Sniper the Cat are recommended.

